_site/
.sass-cache/
.jekyll-metadata
# Python bytecode from analysis scripts
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Spent one-off migrations. update-towns-format.py rewrote nny-toponyms.html
# from one TOWNS data shape to another on 2026-03-22; it is not idempotent —
# a second run would double-wrap the entries it already converted.
_resources/update-towns-format.py

# Obsidian vault config — this repo is opened as a vault for writing posts.
# Workspace layout, plugin state and cache; none of it belongs on the site.
.obsidian/

# Symlink to the private sessions repo — see backlog/site.md there.
# This repo is PUBLIC; an internal backlog must not be committed to it.
BACKLOG.md

# _ideas/ is SCRATCH, and this repo is PUBLIC. Anything in there — half-formed
# posts, working notes, TODO comments addressed to me by name — is published on
# github.com the moment it is committed, even though Jekyll never builds the
# directory. The narrow `*-draft.md` rule this replaces was a half-measure: it
# depended on naming discipline, and a name-based rule goes silently inert the
# moment a file is named differently.
#
# `_ideas/*` and NOT `_ideas/`. Excluding the directory itself stops git
# descending into it, which makes every negation below unreachable — the classic
# silently-inert gitignore. Excluding its CONTENTS keeps the door open so an
# exception can be carved out.
_ideas/*
# The one exception, because PUBLISHING.md documents a workflow that names this
# file (`cp _ideas/typography-specimen.html _site/` after each build) and it is
# the canonical demonstration of the site's marks. It is a reference artifact,
# not scratch.
!_ideas/typography-specimen.html

# Cache + intermediate for script/build-sdud-map.py; the result is embedded
# in the page, so neither needs to be tracked.
script/states-10m.json
script/usmap.json
